      "title": "Small temperature difference, short residence time",
      "description": "Steam condenses outside the tubes while a thin film of liquid flows down the inside walls by gravity and evaporates from its surface. Because the film is thin and there is no hydrostatic head, it works with small temperature differences and very short residence time — ideal for heat-sensitive products such as milk, juices and pharmaceuticals.",
