  "summary": "In a falling film evaporator the liquid is distributed at the top of long vertical tubes and flows down the inside walls as a thin film, heated by steam condensing outside. Vapour and concentrate leave at the bottom and are split in a separator. Short residence time and small temperature differences suit heat-sensitive products.",
